      "writtenOn": "2025-05-20T20:07:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we haven\u0027t done discovery yet, and we\u0027re connected a PD 3.x partner, we should return `SVDM_VER_2_1` as a default. If we\u0027re asking this question, it will be because we\u0027re about to send Discover Identity. Once it comes back, we\u0027ll set `svdm_vers`, and we\u0027ll use that for the next VDM we send.\n\nAs discussed out of band, SVDM version 2.1 should be our default here, because _we_ implement PD r3.2. We have no real way of telling whether the partner is implementing, for example, PD r3.1 or PD r3.2 without sending Get_Revision. The partner emulator won\u0027t respond to Get_Revision, so it wouldn\u0027t matter for these tests anyway. When we downgrade our SVDM version from 2.1 to 2.0, it should be based on the partner\u0027s SVDM version, and we already have logic for that.",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "35bc2b44_e6899c4d",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 700,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 703,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\t/*\n\t\t * If we haven\u0027t done discovery yet, and we\u0027re connected a PD 3.x\n\t\t * partner, we should return SVDM_VER_2_1 as a default. If we\u0027re\n\t\t * asking this question, it will be because we\u0027re about to send\n\t\t * Discover Identity.\n\t\t */\n"
            },
