      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just FYI, `data` will be a pointer to whatever the fixture type is of the calling test, and you\u0027re using this function with multiple suites, which means multiple fixture types. This isn\u0027t a problem right now, because 1) you\u0027re not dereferencing the pointer, and 2) the structs happen to have the same definition anyway. But just be aware that if you added a field to one of these structs and accessed it here, this function would have undefined behavior for the other test.\n\nI\u0027d prefer that we never use functions like this, but the alternative is more test boilerplate, and the compiler doesn\u0027t catch it, so you\u0027ll probably find quite a few instances of this pattern.",
      "revId": "d219111558fc7f85fc55b7dca8c0987884b3ab95",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
